import Mathlib

/-!
# OEIS A101208: smallest odd prime p with n = (p - 1) / ord_p(2)

Source: https://oeis.org/A101208 (OEIS Foundation, CC BY-SA 4.0)
Credit: @sntntHb

A101208 gives, for `n ≥ 1`, the smallest odd prime `p` such that `n = (p - 1) / ord_p(2)`,
where `ord_p(2)` is the multiplicative order of 2 modulo `p` (so `ord_p(2)` divides `p - 1`
and `(p - 1) / ord_p(2)` is the index of the subgroup generated by 2). The entry states:

  Conjecture: a(n) is defined for all n.

We formalize: for every `n ≥ 1` there is an odd prime `p` with `p - 1 = n * ord_p(2)`,
where `ord_p(2)` is `orderOf (2 : ZMod p)`.
-/

namespace OMA.S_oeis_a101208

/-- Conjecture of A101208: every positive integer is the index `(p - 1) / ord_p(2)` of 2
modulo some odd prime `p`. -/
theorem main : ∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n →
    ∃ p : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ p ≠ 2 ∧ p - 1 = n * orderOf (2 : ZMod p) := by
  sorry

end OMA.S_oeis_a101208
